{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/245024-adding-athletics-to-defense","id":245024,"title":"Adding Athletics to Defense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-30T15:26:12-07:00","id":245024,"title":"Adding Athletics to Defense","content":"Hi guys, I've been a storyteller for Vampire the Masquerade since 1992 and then I lost it a little since the Requism edition which was great IMO but lost some momentum. I'm back in the saddle with Blood and Smoke edition and I love most changes made to the previous edition BUT something is being a bit iffy to me: adding athletics to the defense rating. I'm afraid that it would be overkill are make combats too long. Any feedback from those who tested this rule ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T15:52:50-07:00","id":245044,"title":"","content":"From what I have experienced, it doesn't change combat too drastically. The reason for this is because even though you hit less often, you hit significantly harder if you do. For example, under the old rules if you have a strength of 3, weaponry of 3, and a 2L dagger, you would roll 8 dice contested by the opponents defense.<br /> <br /> Now, you would only roll 6 dice instead of 8, but if you succeed, you deal success in damage + automatic successes due to the weapon<br /> <br /> If you are not using a weapon, then yes, fights will take longer since you are trying to punch someone to death and/or submission which is far harder to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T17:29:01-07:00","id":245078,"title":"","content":"The increased Defense is, generally, going to be a bit behind offense. Even if the two are much closer and a character built right can be a successful defensive fighter than most opponents. Expect most attack pools in the 1-4 range amongst fairly even combat investments unless the defender Dodges.<br /> <br /> So yeah, as Dessembrae said, less hits, but harder hits with the new damage rules.<br /> <br /> And grappling was revised to go a bit faster as well. Though striking with Brawl without supernatural weapons, Merits, or some such can be pretty slow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T18:03:14-07:00","id":245111,"title":"","content":"I have to say, particularly with Vampires in the 2e rules, Grapple can be really, really deadly once it's established. Those folks with rolls lowered by Defense can really do a lot of Damage when using the Damage move, whether they have a weapon or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T18:10:06-07:00","id":245113,"title":"","content":"You have Down and Dirty Combat (p 176) if you want to eliminate long combats. The playtests I read indicated it can be long when combat focused characters with lots of experience, but otherwise it is usually quick. Two characters that are an equal match should go on for a bit if they are really geared for combat, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:33:39-07:00","id":245156,"title":"","content":"You also have the Beaten Down and Stun rules to consider. Inflicting either of these can easily end a fight. Beaten Down can keep fights that aren't about harming/killing the other guy as hard as possible short, and Stun will make your next round pretty likely to be a fight ending hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T23:57:35-07:00","id":245208,"title":"","content":"And the called shots to legs, arms, hands etc. are all worth a look, especially if you've got a poor dice pool as the -4 to hit a hand when you're rolling few dice rarely makes a difference (-1 is the same as -50 dice) and landing that blow can bring your opponent down to your level pretty quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T18:57:53-07:00","id":245768,"title":"","content":"Thanks you all for your inputs. I will give it a chance and test it. I see the point about hitting dealing more damage now. Still, with celerity you should be able to reach a 7 or 8 defense quite easily. Called shots and Grapple are probably even more interesting under these rules, I'll try this too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T21:57:29-07:00","id":245879,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that you can easily have a 7-8 dice pool to attack, and then Vigor to counteract Celerity if you're an offensive build. Vigor 3 means +3 dice to hit, and you can spend blood to increase your damage for the turn... Vigor 3, a 3L weapon, and even 1 success is 7 damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T14:24:36-07:00","id":246363,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm concerned about several things (but I will test the current rules nonetheless): the length of combat, the ability to deal an exceptional success (which, it seems to me, has melted into nothingness), the abilities of my players to actually hit another combat orientated vampire (not to say a Mage but I won't go into this). Yeah disciplines can counter one another (especially Vigor in this case) but I got a feeling that under the current rules you'd better being prepared for narrative combat: players (and NPCS alike) would better come up with ideas and tricks to get themselves the additional dice bonus that would make all the difference. And, it doesn't sound bad, it does sound worth testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 09-01-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T15:43:41-07:00","id":246392,"title":"","content":"Exceptional successes willbe rare indeed, but as their &quot;place&quot; is sorta taken by Tilts that can be inflicted by less than 5 successes (ussually), that's not something to be worried about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:20:41-08:00","id":774895,"title":"","content":"I actually gave it a try but, you see when I read rules, I'm very analytical, but when I'm Storytelling I'm more freeform and therefore it works for me but the combat system now is a little slow for my taste and I tend to have an general look at a situation and dice results and taking it from here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:48:07-08:00","id":774906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/245024-adding-athletics-to-defense?p=246363#post246363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I got a feeling that under the current rules you'd better being prepared for narrative combat: players (and NPCS alike) would better come up with ideas and tricks to get themselves the additional dice bonus that would make all the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an accurate assessment, and from what I can tell, the designer's intent. Fights where two combatants take turns rolling dice at each other in an empty featureless room will be a slog. Fights where multiple combatants focus their attacks on a single target, employ techniques like grappling, targeted attacks, spend willpower, use physical intensity, Frenzy, use the terrain to their advantage, and employ dirty tricks to get ST fiat bonuses will be dynamic, interesting, and won't take terribly long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:17:37-08:00","id":775027,"title":"","content":"In my experience I find the fight pretty funny and balanced. Unarmed combat are obviously slower, as in the reality. Weaponed combat are faster and in a couple of hit ( as mortal and without consider resilence or healing) you kill your opponents. If the fight is not important you can go with &quot;Down and Dirty combat rules&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T15:29:31-08:00","id":775063,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that due to Physical Intensity and blood healing, your base defense and attack pools are secondary to question &quot;how much I'm willing to burn in order to bring this guy down&quot;. Vamps that don't have special combat tricks that can cheat in lethal or aggravated damage on their opponents should be probably less concerned with their health bar and defense rating and more with &quot;is this fight worth being hungry and potentially weakened for the night&quot;. <br /> This of course depends a lot on how popular fights to the true death are in your games; current rules support situations where physical conflict is quite popular, but rarely taken to extreme. Read - you can totally have two vampires demolishing a bar and ripping each other to shreds only for one them to call &quot;Bob, I'm out, I'm getting hungry, this is not worth it&quot;. Again, this is good from players point of view, because it means that you can engage into physical conflicts without having to fear too much about your character getting accidentally axed, like mortals do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:05:03-08:00","id":775501,"title":"","content":"In actual play, I've found that in 2nd edition fights between unskilled, unarmed combatants are much longer, but fights between skilled, armed, supernatural combatants can be much, much shorter.<br /> <br /> Which kind of makes sense. Two teenagers in a brawl in the schoolyard? That can go on for a long time without one seriously injuring the other. Two special forces dudes with knives? Even if equally matched, once one gets an advantage it'll be over fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T11:01:40-08:00","id":775554,"title":"","content":"One-on-one fights can also be slow, but when a group gangs up on one poor sap, it's over very quickly. Which, again, makes logical sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T13:21:18-08:00","id":775607,"title":"","content":"The most interesting side effect of the new combat rules, combined with the bigger punch of the physical Disciplines, is that vampires really, really shouldn't fight each other. It's very all or nothing and costly, and unless you explicitly know the fight isn't to the death (no guarantee under the spectre of frenzy) it's often better to either let it go or find a more diplomatic solution. Kindred society depends on it. When you throw down, it better be worth it...<br /> <br /> Fighting humans on the other hand? Well, that's what they call &quot;hunting&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-27-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T13:38:06-08:00","id":775612,"title":"","content":"I find Lashing Out is a nice, nonlethal substitute that allows people to show off dominance without having to focus in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}